1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,192
Mullvad Browser Extension: Chrome MV3 build in Chromium (Mullvad WireGuard runs in a network namespace)

2
00:00:05,192 --> 00:00:08,695
Baseline: connected through Mullvad WireGuard (se-sto-wg-001, Sweden)

3
00:00:08,695 --> 00:00:17,551
Extension popup: connection check shows the Mullvad exit, DNS servers and a WebRTC check

4
00:00:17,551 --> 00:00:22,950
Options page: proxies need the optional "tabs" + "all sites" permissions

5
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:28,767
Granting permissions with Chrome's native prompt

6
00:00:28,767 --> 00:00:42,705
Popup > All websites > Select location > Switzerland

7
00:00:42,705 --> 00:00:47,516
Global proxy set: the popup now reports a Zurich exit (SOCKS5 via the PAC script)

8
00:00:47,516 --> 00:00:54,629
Reloading am.i.mullvad.net: exit is now a Swiss Mullvad SOCKS5 server

9
00:00:54,629 --> 00:01:11,505
Per-site proxy: ipinfo.io > Current domain > Select location > Japan

10
00:01:11,505 --> 00:01:19,816
ipinfo.io now exits in Japan, while other sites keep using Switzerland

11
00:01:19,816 --> 00:01:36,552
Second per-site proxy: ip-api.com > Select location > USA

12
00:01:36,552 --> 00:01:43,938
ip-api.com now exits in the USA

13
00:01:43,938 --> 00:01:52,435
Rules also apply to subdomains: www.ipinfo.io uses the ipinfo.io rule (Japan)

14
00:01:52,435 --> 00:01:59,598
Sites without a rule still use the global Swiss proxy

15
00:01:59,598 --> 00:02:11,933
Excluding a site: ifconfig.co is proxied through Switzerland...

16
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:15,818
...Current domain > Never proxy

17
00:02:15,818 --> 00:02:23,116
ifconfig.co now goes direct: the WireGuard exit in Stockholm

18
00:02:23,116 --> 00:02:34,157
Random mode: each site gets its own random Mullvad proxy (stable for the session)

19
00:02:34,157 --> 00:02:41,295
Random mode: am.i.mullvad.net

20
00:02:41,295 --> 00:02:48,168
Random mode: ipinfo.io

21
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:54,289
Random mode: ip-api.com

22
00:02:54,289 --> 00:03:01,234
Random mode off again

23
00:03:01,234 --> 00:03:20,853
Leak checks with the Swiss global proxy: DNS is resolved by Mullvad through the proxy

24
00:03:20,853 --> 00:03:28,654
The popup flags WebRTC exposing the tunnel IP (WebRTC is not proxied by default)

25
00:03:28,654 --> 00:03:35,897
Options > Settings: turn the WebRTC switch off (webRTCIPHandlingPolicy = disable_non_proxied_udp)

26
00:03:35,897 --> 00:03:47,913
WebRTC no longer leaks any IP

27
00:03:47,913 --> 00:03:58,197
Options > Proxy: all configured per-site proxies and exclusions

28
00:03:58,197 --> 00:04:02,748
Options > Import/Export: settings can be exported and imported as JSON

29
00:04:02,748 --> 00:04:05,780
Options > About

30
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:09,282
Done: global, per-site, excluded and random proxies via a PAC script on Chrome MV3
